": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The test expectations match ROUND_HALF_EVEN: 2.675 rounds to 2.68 (7 is odd, so it goes to the even neighbour) and 2.665 rounds to 2.66. The bug is that `src/money.py` uses ROUND_HALF_UP. I'll create the branch and make that one-line fix.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01FJDihP3h1tDb2uqzGoSRRX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/round-half-even-fin-212", "from_ref": "main"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_017VjJb52Wvniv5A42iW7Qsu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/round-half-even-fin-212", "message": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (banker's rounding) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0126AM83YBYvVmJCeANfCdcB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/round-half-even-fin-212", "idempotency_key": "fix-round-half-even-fin-212-ci-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01JetZfCH5zCBGbgKrPNKRzX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "CI passed on the branch. Next I'll open the pull request against main, requesting review from alex. I won't merge it, since merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_019Mi6cTTMYFagHLQ2jSUoXS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/round-half-even-fin-212", "base": "main", "title": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (banker's rounding) in round_money per FIN-212", "body": "Fixes the nightly build failure in tests/test_money.py.\n\n`round_money` was documented as using banker's rounding per FIN-212 but was implemented with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. This changes the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, which matches the docstring and the test expectations:\n\n- `round_money(Decimal(\"2.675\")) == Decimal(\"2.68\")`\n- `round_money(Decimal(\"2.665\")) == Decimal(\"2.66\")`\n\nCI on `fix/round-half-even-fin-212` (08d3cd5986): passed.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "fix-round-half-even-fin-212-pr"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the nightly failure and opened PR #101 against main, with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but the docstring and FIN-212 call for banker's rounding. The test expectations match ROUND_HALF_EVEN: 2.675 \u2192 2.68 and 2.665 \u2192 2.66.\n- **Change:** On branch `fix/round-half-even-fin-212`, I switched the rounding mode in `src/money.py` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** The run on commit 08d3cd5986 passed.\n- **PR:** #101, \"Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (banker's rounding) in round_money per FIN-212\", from the fix branch into main.\n\nI did not merge it. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner.", "type": "text"}]}]}